1
00:00:00,180 --> 00:00:01,230
Natural.

2
00:00:01,230 --> 00:00:02,000
Multigrain.

3
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:03,320
No added sugar.

4
00:00:03,320 --> 00:00:04,980
They sound healthy... right?

5
00:00:04,980 --> 00:00:06,910
Let's turn the pack around.

6
00:00:06,910 --> 00:00:08,250
Natural sounds reassuring.

7
00:00:08,250 --> 00:00:09,440
But it doesn't tell you

8
00:00:09,440 --> 00:00:10,830
how much sugar, salt,

9
00:00:10,830 --> 00:00:12,730
or saturated fat you're getting.

10
00:00:12,730 --> 00:00:15,370
Multigrain just means more than one grain.

11
00:00:15,370 --> 00:00:16,480
Whole grains?

12
00:00:16,480 --> 00:00:17,710
Not necessarily.

13
00:00:17,710 --> 00:00:18,570
Look for whole wheat

14
00:00:18,570 --> 00:00:20,480
or whole oats in the ingredients.

15
00:00:20,480 --> 00:00:22,280
No added sugar sounds like sugar-free...

16
00:00:22,280 --> 00:00:23,240
but not quite.

17
00:00:23,240 --> 00:00:24,730
Naturally occurring sugars

18
00:00:24,730 --> 00:00:25,800
can still be there.

19
00:00:25,800 --> 00:00:27,150
Check total sugars, too.

20
00:00:27,150 --> 00:00:28,180
Comparing two packs?

21
00:00:28,180 --> 00:00:29,270
Use the same amount...

22
00:00:29,270 --> 00:00:30,930
like per hundred grams.

23
00:00:30,930 --> 00:00:31,550
Then check how much

24
00:00:31,550 --> 00:00:32,420
you actually eat.

25
00:00:32,420 --> 00:00:33,830
The front gets your attention.

26
00:00:33,830 --> 00:00:35,310
The back helps you choose.

27
00:00:35,310 --> 00:00:35,760
Small habit.

28
00:00:35,760 --> 00:00:36,780
Better information.

29
00:00:36,780 --> 00:00:38,600
Flip it before you pick it.
